  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The marinade called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "chermoula",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chermoula"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " takes 5 minutes to make and transforms plain fish into something completely different. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Scoring fish",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "scoring-fish"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " before marinating allows the spices to penetrate. An hour is sufficient; overnight in the fridge is even better."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Any firm white fish works. Sea bass, cod, hake and mackerel are all excellent. The pan must be hot before the fish goes on, or the skin will stick rather than crisp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
